The '''Confederal Navy''' ({{lang-bl|Armada confederales}}) is the [[w:Navy|naval force]] of the [[Balisca|Baliscan Confederation]], and one of the three branches of the [[Confederal Armed Forces]]. It traces its roots to volunteers and former privateers that sided with the [[Northern Confederation]] in the face of Volisanian attempts at reconquest during the [[Continuation War|Resistencía]]. As of May 2023, the Navy had a strength of over 130,000 active personnel with approximately 160 vessels in service, including minor auxiliary vessels. It is considered a "multi-regional {{W|blue-water navy}}".

The Baliscan Navy emerged from the [[Great Adonian War]] as the one of the world's most powerful navies. In the 21st century, the Baliscan Navy maintains a sizable global {{W|humanitarian aid|humanitarian}} presence, deploying in strength in such areas as the [[Aethiopian Ocean|Aethiopian]], the [[Shendan Ocean|Eastern Shendan]], and the [[Bight of Ayorin]]. It maintains the ability to respond rapidly to situations in littoral areas of the wider Kafto-Abyalan region. It engages in forward port calls during peacetime, making it a frequent actor in Baliscan [[International relations of Balisca|diplomatic and humanitarian policy]].

