=== Naming conventions ===
Ships of the Confederal Navy are named per [[Naval Vessels Naming Initiative]] that was first adopted on 7 November 1940, and subsequently revised most recently on 20 November 2015. The convention for naming naval ships is as follows;

* Aircraft carriers are named after mountains.
* Nuclear-powered submarines are all named after regions.
* Destroyers and frigates are named after cities.
* Tank landing ships and dock landing ships carry the names of cantons.
* Smaller anti-submarine ships are named for seamounts.
* Infantry landing ships are named for rivers.
* Replenishment ships are named for lakes.

